2026-09-20 00:00:07,304 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The primary digital system associated with the investigation (the 'pc' image) contains evidence of user activities highly relevant to data exfiltration. Multiple files show name/content mismatches, such as PNG files with JPEG content and an HTML file with GZIP compression, a common technique to bypass simple content inspection. The registry analysis shows the user installed cloud storage tools (iCloud and Google Drive) on 2015-03-23, and later executed Google Drive Sync (googledrivesync.exe) on 2015-03-25. The user also launched data cleaning utilities (CCleaner and Eraser), suggesting an intent to conceal activity. Browser history reveals searches for cloud storage services on the same day the tools were installed. While no active files from the project (like 'secret_project]_proposal.docx') are being accessed via UserAssist, the user interacted with 'Secret Project Data' folders in Windows Explorer on 2015-03-24, indicating recent access. The system also shows evidence of an external USB storage device being connected, which could have been used for data transfer. Although an archive file ('winter_whether_advisory.zip') was found in the $OrphanFiles directory, it is not linked to the optical media in the current evidence, and no direct connection between the USB device or cloud sync activity and the optical media has been established. Therefore, while the user accessed the data and had tools to exfilter it, the evidence does not confirm that the Secret Project Data was copied to the optical media.
